Top 30 Scenario-Based REST API Interview Questions (Senior Developer)

These are the kinds of questions typically asked for 13+ years Java/Spring Boot/Microservices profiles.

1. API Design Scenario
Question

You need to design APIs for a banking system to manage customers and accounts. How would you design the endpoints?

Expected Answer
Use resource-oriented URLs
GET    /customers/{id}
POST   /customers
PUT    /customers/{id}

GET    /customers/{id}/accounts
POST   /customers/{id}/accounts

Interview One-Liner
REST APIs should model business resources, not actions.
2. Duplicate Request Scenario
Question

Client accidentally calls fund transfer API twice. How will you prevent duplicate transfers?

Expected Answer
Use Idempotency Key
Store request reference
Return same response for duplicate request
Idempotency-Key: TXN12345

Interview One-Liner
Financial APIs should support idempotency to prevent duplicate transactions.
